Byline is a modified version of humanizer. What changed: the writing patterns were rewritten as
rule files with generic examples and split into shared rules and each person's own rules; check,
review, flag and setup modes were added; and the checks were added as a separate program written
in Go. The original copyright line and licence are kept unchanged in LICENSE.

2. Wikipedia's "Signs of AI writing" guide
The idea for Byline's pattern list comes from Wikipedia's guide "Signs of AI writing" (WikiProject
AI Cleanup, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Signs_of_AI_writing); Byline's text and
examples are its own.
